    "title": "What channel is Astros vs. Angels game on? How to watch Friday",
    "text": "Mike Trout and the Angels will face Joey Loperfido and the Astros in the second of the teams' four-game series Friday, but it'll require a streaming subscription to watch.Jason Fochtman/Houston ChronicleOne day into the Houston Astros' season and fans will have to navigate MLB’s byzantine national TV packages.Friday’s 7:15 p.m. game against the Los Angeles Angels at Daikin Park will not be broadcast or streamed on Space City Home Network, the Astros' usual carrier.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢Instead, the game will stream exclusively on Apple TV to kick off the streamer’s fifth season of MLB Friday night games. An Apple TV subscription is required to watch. A subscription costs $12.99 a month plus tax, with a free seven-day trial offered to qualified new and returning subscribers. Article continues below this adAlex Faust (play-by-play), Ryan Spilborghs (analyst) and Tricia Whitaker (field reporter) will call the game. Friday is one of two Apple TV games for the Astros during the first half of the schedule. The May 22 game in Chicago against the Cubs, with a 1:20 p.m. first pitch at Wrigley Field, also is an Apple exclusive.Houston Chronicle LogoMake us a Preferred Source on Google to see more of us when you search.Add Preferred SourceThe Astros have one other scheduled streaming exclusive this season: the July 5 home game against Tampa Bay that will air on Peacock at 2:30 p.m. as part of “Star Spangled Sunday” on NBC and Peacock, which joined MLB’s group of national rightsholders this season.Article continues below this ad",
